name: vigo-secrets-perms-retract
description: >-
  Retraction module for vigo-secrets-perms. Nothing meaningful to undo —
  the install module enforces mode 0600 + root:root ownership, which is
  also the right default. Leaving the secret-vault files restrictive on
  retract is safer than relaxing them. Comments below name the install
  resources so the operator can see what was being enforced.

resources: []

# Install resources that needed no retraction:
#   directory: secrets-dir-perms       — leave at 0700; needed by vigosrv
#   exec:      master-key-perms        — leave at 0600; correct default
#   exec:      master-verifier-perms   — leave at 0600; correct default
